#{[{:activity/expected-seconds 900.0 :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120695} :activity/id #uuid "ad4d6410-a365-5f77-a4b1-3e2d134d5a3d" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050638 :topic/id #uuid "5ae18ce0-90c2-55f7-8d81-bd5949f05aa3" :topic/math-academy-id 1864} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120695 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186121042 :tutorial/content "Given a subspace $H$ with a basis $\\mathcal B = \\{ \\mathbf b_1, \\mathbf b_2 \\}$ and a vector $\\mathbf x \\in H,$ the **coordinates of the vector** $\\mathbf{x}$ **relative to the basis** $\\mathcal{B}$ are the coefficients ${\\color{red} x_1}$ and ${\\color{blue} x_2}$ such that\n\n$$\n{\\color{red}x_1} \\mathbf{b}_1+{\\color{blue}x_2} \\mathbf{b}_2 = \\mathbf{x}.\n$$\n\nWe can write the vector $\\mathbf x$ relative to the basis $\\mathcal B$ using these coordinates, as follows:\n\n![](images/05/0593ca6a838b66c4623e8749eb5236d6259b1f9bf36ed0d68b83c49781076341.svg)\n\nTo demonstrate, consider the basis $\\mathcal{B}=\\{ \\mathbf{b}_1, \\mathbf{b}_2 \\},$ where \n\n![](images/f3/f355faa0c477775f2a1cbb3522d0743cdbc9649a5ee9c55b579b1fac9ae2a661.svg)\n\nAlso let $H = \\textrm{span} \\{ \\mathbf b_1, \\mathbf b_2 \\},$ and consider the vector ![](images/78/78357fcf51c9cd6b7873f5bc35fcc214cb3790bcec00ee69d0932f15aacd39cb.svg)\n\nThe vector $\\mathbf x$ can be expressed as a unique linear combination of $\\mathbf b_1$ and $\\mathbf b_2.$ That is to say, there exist *unique coefficients* $\\color{red}x_1$ and $\\color{blue}x_2$ such that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{b}_{1}+{x}_{2}{b}_{2} & =x \\\\ {x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's solve for these coefficients. From the above, we get the following system:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=8 \\\\ 2{x}_{2}=4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe unique solution of this system is \n\n![](images/82/82d4f494936d23e9b697aa4518edf68f7ea62e504d9d2576a6d13971acaf1c96.svg)\n\nTherefore, we have that \n\n$$\n\\mathbf{x} = {\\color{red}3} \\mathbf{b}_1+ {\\color{blue}2} \\mathbf{b}_2,\n$$\n\nwhich can be visualized as shown below.\n\n![](images/94/94b2934727a32284e9790e59ccd301bd858a0258843314a2968285a5eda7a302.png)" :tutorial/id #uuid "bb4f07e6-7c2f-5fe2-b96b-1bb37603981a" :tutorial/math-academy-id 3208 :tutorial/title "Introduction"} :step/id #uuid "55354f89-d587-5329-9788-b198ebb218a3" :step/math-academy-id 17513 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120696}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120696 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119820 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119631 :question/id #uuid "0a0ea798-5125-5d0e-a755-96bf9af5f543" :question/math-academy-id "e-4823"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6e4f1675-9146-5279-9b64-07a63a9bed99" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048499}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120379} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120382} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186247247} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186319177} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186319186} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186391910} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186393563} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186409817} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186430732}] :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Vector Given Its Coordinates Relative To a Given Basis"} :step/id #uuid "b2734184-6a42-50f6-9a19-566236b06025" :step/math-academy-id 17514 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120757}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120697 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119821 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119632 :question/id #uuid "6c7237cd-c655-575f-83ac-7a0891c336b2" :question/math-academy-id "e-4824"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "841f498b-f737-5086-8f79-44f1a143bebb" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120352} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120380} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186247252} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186319175} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186319176} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186345154} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186386599} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186391903} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186409818} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186409820} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186416946} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186426857} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186430731}] :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Coordinates of a Vector Relative To a Given Basis Containing Two Vectors"} :step/id #uuid "94aa1ebf-d415-58aa-a0dc-17e8201c1669" :step/math-academy-id 17515 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120698}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120698 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119822 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119633 :question/id #uuid "90f07e38-405a-5f79-8501-0b4dfb8fa4c8" :question/math-academy-id "e-4825"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ed6a6ea8-6100-5224-b75f-b87c037fafbb" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120357} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120358} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186247255} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186247256} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186247257} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186320959} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186345167} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186409821} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186426856} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186455442} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186455505}] :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Coordinates of a Vector Relative To a Given Basis Containing More Than Two Vectors"} :step/id #uuid "34b75a42-9505-5418-a27f-2b9aade2bc07" :step/math-academy-id 17516 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120756}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120756 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186121066 :tutorial/content "Let's consider a set of vectors\n![](images/0d/0d78e1b2d01003885882f19b3856278e5024719f26f33594fd071fbd73273b71.svg)\n\nNotice that the set $\\mathcal{S}$ is linearly independent since the vector equation $x_1\\mathbf{e}_1+x_2\\mathbf{e}_2+x_3\\mathbf{e}_3=\\mathbf{0}$ leads to the system\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}=0 \\\\ {x}_{2}=0 \\\\ {x}_{3}=0,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich has only the zero solution. \n\nAlso, notice that any vector in $\\mathbb{R}^3$ can be written as a linear combination of $\\mathbf{e}_1,$ $\\mathbf{e}_2,$ and $\\mathbf{e}_3.$ For instance,\n![](images/ef/ef28dd8cbad6d256b9fa82c487263af3327ce630839cfcd1c7433417d0e0ae73.svg)\n\nIn particular, the equation above tells us that \n![](images/72/724f42afb534edbde7588c5508a4bf8de6d3cd068bc2989da7c7207b1bf7a1ba.svg)\nthat is to say, the numbers $\\color{red}-2,$ $\\color{red}0,$ $\\color{red}5$ are the coordinates of $\\mathbf{v}$ relative to the basis $\\mathcal{S}.$ \n\nThe basis $\\mathcal{S}$ is somewhat special, since the coordinates of a vector relative to this basis coincide with the components of the vector. We refer to $\\mathcal{S}$ as the **standard basis**. Remember that in $\\mathbb{R}^2$ and $\\mathbb{R}^3$ we even have special notations for the vectors of the standard basis:\n![](images/ae/aee5dd3226ebe950defc8b873399a884e0679ce701a3a55354ef01960e029f8e.svg)\n\n![](images/dd/dd96e0b70173adf8983feb4975c351ab3e417c34ed4a6a944bc391e33db4c8e9.png)\n\nIn general, the standard basis of $\\mathbb{R}^n$ is\n\n![](images/a8/a8e4b648898c0dc036e228fb84945833dc40c053beff034596e098c4dd077e23.svg)" :tutorial/id #uuid "54e7c1fd-c7bf-5c77-bcc5-eb8d93a11582" :tutorial/math-academy-id 3969 :tutorial/title "The Standard Basis"} :step/id #uuid "9053925c-8744-5312-b890-f5e4a1a8d2e8" :step/math-academy-id 23574} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120757 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119859 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119674 :question/id #uuid "a79126f2-e26c-5929-93d8-825d85b9a438" :question/math-academy-id "e-6282"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a2926764-dfbc-5e4e-a6b0-db24a7298a64" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120525} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120526} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186247248} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186247249} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186247250} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186345146} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186345147} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186345150} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186345152} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186409819}] :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Coordinates of a Vector Relative To a Given Basis by Inspection"} :step/id #uuid "79095f38-ffd3-565b-a534-f136c7646422" :step/math-academy-id 23612 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120697}}] :activity/title "Expressing the Coordinates of a Vector in a Given Basis" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :activity.type/lesson} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186120054}] [{:activity/course {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186046673} :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186416947} :activity/id #uuid "e9bd4727-090c-5259-8cb9-53f91a718d53" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050638 :topic/id #uuid "5ae18ce0-90c2-55f7-8d81-bd5949f05aa3" :topic/math-academy-id 1864} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186416947 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186416946 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "54b2da92-80e1-5a61-a19c-e0402c5db36e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416936} {:answer/id #uuid "94ec8a9d-591d-59ec-b9c5-a655500ebc04" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416937} {:answer/id #uuid "c791cf81-feb5-59a1-bf25-b0be74c138f2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x\\notin \\text{span}{{b}_{1},{b}_{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416940} {:answer/id #uuid "ccdbeb50-bd46-5e6a-a5d9-d2fa3f1bb293" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416942} {:answer/id #uuid "f2716f4b-b756-5daf-b7ff-420d367fb480" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416943}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186416936} :answer-field/id #uuid "9bd25317-6ae7-5ed2-b2f8-06a74441129a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416944}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "1098aac8-90b3-5ba0-b447-7ead2947d568" :question/math-academy-id "q-35247" :question/problem "Find the coordinates of the vector $x$ relative to the basis $B={{b}_{1},{b}_{2}},$ where\n\n$$\n{b}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 9 \\\\ -12\\end{aligned}],\\,{b}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ -8 \\\\ 16\\end{aligned}],\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}-8 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 32\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]$ then what is the value of ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}?$" :question/worked-solution "We need to find ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ such that  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{b}_{1}+{x}_{2}{b}_{2} & =x \\\\ {x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 9 \\\\ -12\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ -8 \\\\ 16\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-8 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 32\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe equation above gives the system with the augmented matrix \n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}3 & -4 & -8 \\\\ 9 & -8 & -4 \\\\ -12 & 16 & 32\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nRow-reducing the matrix using Gaussian elimination, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & -4 & -8 \\\\ 9 & -8 & -4 \\\\ -12 & 16 & 32\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}3 & -4 & -8 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 20 \\\\ -12 & 16 & 32\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+4{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}3 & -4 & -8 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 20 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}3{x}_{1}-4{x}_{2}=-8 \\\\ 4{x}_{2}=20.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get ${x}_{2}=5.$ Substituting this into the first equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n3{x}_{1}-4(5)=-8\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=4.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}].$\n\nFinally, ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=4+5=9.$"} :step/id #uuid "52d64f85-27e5-5e6b-8c92-f165572fe095" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186416948}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186416948 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120525 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "04f5fc79-efcf-5beb-8f44-6c5bbee2e205" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x\\notin \\text{Span}{{b}_{1},{b}_{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416934} {:answer/id #uuid "460c227b-da50-5240-a61b-5d7158cbefb0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416935} {:answer/id #uuid "b96e7099-61f5-552d-a37f-75ea4d0acd7b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416938} {:answer/id #uuid "c28d8b2c-0794-5b52-be1a-1a5068c24206" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416939} {:answer/id #uuid "ca59db9a-208c-56e6-9d14-d390aecd3368" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416941}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186416935} :answer-field/id #uuid "c652bfa5-8e6a-53fc-ad6f-da352c6f194d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416945}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "93dd069a-4710-5057-b8fe-736d3ab4c0dc" :question/math-academy-id "q-75844" :question/problem "Find the coordinates of the vector $x$ relative to the basis $B={{b}_{1},{b}_{2}},$ where\n\n$$\n{b}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{b}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]$ then what is the value of ${x}_{2}?$" :question/worked-solution "Remember, the order of the vectors in a basis is important.\n\nNotice that \n\n$$\n{{[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{x}={{(\\,2\\,)}_{⏟}}_{{x}_{1}}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{b}_{1}}+{{(\\,-4\\,)}_{⏟}}_{{x}_{2}}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{b}_{2}}\n$$\n\nwhich means that\n\n$$\nx=2\\cdot {b}_{1}+(-4)\\cdot {b}_{2}\n$$\n\nand therefore\n\n$$\n[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFinally, we have that ${x}_{2}=-4.$"} :step/id #uuid "598de137-99ae-5ba2-ac49-2dd82ea7ee2f" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186416949}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186416949 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186409821 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0470cd3b-2bcb-575e-9def-d43004406207" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186409787} {:answer/id #uuid "a3e208c3-ba1a-51ec-b367-c2784fabe06c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186409800} {:answer/id #uuid "a5ba42a7-b00b-5980-9f89-48160c1eb49e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x\\notin \\text{Span}{{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{b}_{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186409801} {:answer/id #uuid "d13c159c-f442-5933-a821-d94880c3ba32" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186409806} {:answer/id #uuid "eec553dd-6fd7-5208-9292-850213e9c19b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186409809}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186409801} :answer-field/id #uuid "a79bee7d-12b6-5017-ae13-ca00a861bd24" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186409812}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "ec45397c-5ced-5a47-b9a9-86c6aa1d1bf3" :question/math-academy-id "q-76073" :question/problem "Find the coordinates of the vector $x$ relative to the basis $B={{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{b}_{3}},$ where\n\n$$\n{b}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,{b}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,{b}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]$ then what is the value of ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}?$" :question/worked-solution "We need to find ${x}_{1}$,  ${x}_{2}$, and ${x}_{3}$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{b}_{1}+{x}_{2}{b}_{2}+{x}_{3}{b}_{3} & =x \\\\ {x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{3}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom this, we get the system with the augmented matrix $M$, which we reduce using Gaussian elimination:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M= & [\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 0 & 5 \\\\ -1 & 0 & -1 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+{R}_{1} \\\\ ∼ & [\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+{R}_{2} \\\\ ∼ & [\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}\\,\\,{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}=5 \\\\ \\,\\,-{x}_{2}-{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ \\,\\,0=5,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere the third equation is always false. Therefore, the system has no solution and we conclude that \n\n$$\nx\\notin \\text{Span}{{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{b}_{3}}.\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "6074dbdf-0c2f-509e-aa43-e4c385bf7861"}] :activity/title "Expressing the Coordinates of a Vector in a Given Basis" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416933}] [{:activity/course {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186046659} :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186426858} :activity/id #uuid "7b9fccdb-a888-5b80-9f71-5e4ef95dcf8c" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050638 :topic/id #uuid "5ae18ce0-90c2-55f7-8d81-bd5949f05aa3" :topic/math-academy-id 1864} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186426858 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186426856 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0e83f3a8-e73e-5dcd-ac90-e7fbd7a63237" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426844} {:answer/id #uuid "1298c82b-5f34-5b3d-9a2e-19a4db3c3122" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426845} {:answer/id #uuid "6f2c222c-23e3-58cc-87ec-9f7920cb1f7d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426847} {:answer/id #uuid "b92f0488-96a7-580a-9581-5603eab3169c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426851} {:answer/id #uuid "ef9d08f1-fc9e-5876-bc5a-62f5443e92fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x\\notin \\text{span}\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2}\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426853}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186426845} :answer-field/id #uuid "3659e401-201b-5665-a817-8016820a5661" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426854}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "973ba0d1-71e0-5bd1-b707-8f3f23076709" :question/math-academy-id "q-34761" :question/problem "Find the coordinates of the vector $x$ relative to the basis $B=\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{b}_{3}\\},$ where\n\n$$\n{b}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,{b}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}],\\,{b}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]$ then what is the value of ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}?$" :question/worked-solution "We need to find ${x}_{1}$,  ${x}_{2}$, and ${x}_{3}$ such that  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{b}_{1}+{x}_{2}{b}_{2}+{x}_{3}{b}_{3} & =x \\\\ {x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{3}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom this, we get the system with the augmented matrix $M$, which we reduce using Gaussian elimination: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M= & [\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & 0 & 6 \\\\ -3 & 0 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -6 & 0 & -6\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1} \\\\ ∼ & [\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & 0 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 12 & 2 & 16 \\\\ 0 & -6 & 0 & -6\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{2} \\\\ ∼ & [\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & 0 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 12 & 2 & 16 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+4{x}_{2}=6 \\\\ 12{x}_{2}+2{x}_{3}=16 \\\\ {x}_{3}=2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the third equation, we get ${x}_{3}=2.$ Substituting this into the second  equation yields\n\n$$\n12{x}_{2}+2(2)=16\\,⟹\\,{x}_{2}=1.\n$$\n\n Finally,  by substituting ${x}_{2}=1$ into the first equation we obtain \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}+4(1)=6\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].$\n\nSo, we have \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}=2+1+2=5.\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "23a4ea36-89a6-56d3-bf56-d577c8099f1a" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186426860}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186426859 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186247257 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6c86a8e6-6f85-5aa5-ae6d-29029bdec356" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245272} {:answer/id #uuid "9aad1bac-86db-5804-9c07-c985acb44877" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245681} {:answer/id #uuid "a44bbdac-4145-547d-a028-c0ec1721745f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245782} {:answer/id #uuid "d577a31d-6124-5fbe-949c-907e0f506fb8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246217} {:answer/id #uuid "f3d6cf3f-5569-5d37-8bae-a5a9fd24ed99" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246466}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186245681} :answer-field/id #uuid "cb99454a-a003-5139-9346-c2529872576e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246914}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "fb853955-e8ef-5657-bd4c-789f3e409e20" :question/math-academy-id "q-112291" :question/problem "Find the coordinates of the vector $x$ relative to the basis $B=\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{b}_{3}\\},$ where\n\n$$\n{b}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}],\\,{b}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}],\\,{b}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}],\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ -15 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]$ then what is the value of ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}?$" :question/worked-solution "We need to find ${x}_{1}$,  ${x}_{2}$, and ${x}_{3}$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{b}_{1}+{x}_{2}{b}_{2}+{x}_{3}{b}_{3} & =x \\\\ {x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{3}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ -15 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom this, we get the system with the augmented matrix $M$, which we reduce using Gaussian elimination:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M= & [\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 0 & 7 \\\\ -2 & -3 & -2 & -15 \\\\ 4 & -2 & -4 & 6\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\ ∼ & [\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 0 & 7 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 4 & -2 & -4 & 6\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-4){R}_{1} \\\\ ∼ & [\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 0 & 7 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -6 & -4 & -22\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-6){R}_{2} \\\\ ∼ & [\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 0 & 7 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 8 & -16\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=7 \\\\ -{x}_{2}-2{x}_{3}=-1 \\\\ 8{x}_{3}=-16.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom third equation we get ${x}_{3}=-2$ and substituting this value into the second equation yields ${x}_{2}=-2(-2)+1=5.$ Finally, substituting ${x}_{2}=5$ into the first equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}+5=7\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}].$\n\nFinally, \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}=2+5+(-2)=5.\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "500d3e2f-f405-56db-9c0b-61c6afc8b340"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186426860 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186345147 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "10b3425c-3f4f-50ac-9c9d-0a2e7c77dbbd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342384} {:answer/id #uuid "429a3619-daf6-5115-8c01-735449d7217d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342791} {:answer/id #uuid "6ca6b908-2e20-5cef-bb8b-aa67933e5937" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343166} {:answer/id #uuid "7becf401-33da-536b-bc10-f41539c33323" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343306} {:answer/id #uuid "868ebaf6-e3a5-54f9-a3a1-db42d06e7646" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343397}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186343397} :answer-field/id #uuid "737ac1c3-2191-5acf-acad-aaac5e91f2b2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344701}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "cfe9fa20-a503-5468-a775-31a4b970b2ec" :question/math-academy-id "q-75973" :question/problem "Find the coordinates of the vector $x$ relative to the basis $B=\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2}\\},$ where\n\n$$\n{b}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{b}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]$ then what is the value of ${x}_{2}?$" :question/worked-solution "Remember, the order of the vectors in a basis is important.\n\nNotice that \n\n$$\n{{[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{x}={{(\\,4\\,)}_{⏟}}_{{x}_{1}}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{b}_{1}}+{{(\\,-3\\,)}_{⏟}}_{{x}_{2}}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{b}_{2}}\n$$\n\nwhich means that\n\n$$\nx=4\\cdot {b}_{1}+(-3)\\cdot {b}_{2}\n$$\n\nand therefore\n\n$$\n[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ \\,\\,-3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFinally, we have that ${x}_{2}=-3.$"} :step/id #uuid "620d8ecf-1f15-5e8d-9b5a-7ce1565395d4" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186426861}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186426861 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186247248 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "41cb02b9-13f3-5f1d-bb94-34c18d18a3a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244889} {:answer/id #uuid "6bdc01cf-2d88-5f1d-918a-b6b8c908df28" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245269} {:answer/id #uuid "7ddf9142-c44c-55fc-9780-62e19815fce1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245422} {:answer/id #uuid "f2a4d81c-2941-5f57-a05a-cf24897f52ce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246455} {:answer/id #uuid "b24cff0c-453c-54bf-b5a0-92ed0ff4ac54" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x\\notin \\text{Span}\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2}\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426850}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186245269} :answer-field/id #uuid "306483a6-036f-5c40-8757-606ab6fe2509" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246624}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "df51ea15-f830-55ce-a2e9-e42267e5f4de" :question/math-academy-id "q-112203" :question/problem "Find the coordinates of the vector $x$ relative to the basis $B=\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2}\\},$ where\n\n$$\n{b}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{b}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 8 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]$ then what is the value of ${x}_{1}?$" :question/worked-solution "Remember, the order of the vectors in a basis is important.\n\nNotice that \n\n$$\n{{[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 8 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{x}={{(\\,3\\,)}_{⏟}}_{{x}_{1}}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{b}_{1}}+{{(\\,8\\,)}_{⏟}}_{{x}_{2}}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{b}_{2}}\n$$\n\nwhich means that\n\n$$\nx=3\\cdot {b}_{1}+8\\cdot {b}_{2}\n$$\n\nand therefore\n\n$$\n[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFinally, we have that ${x}_{1}=3.$"} :step/id #uuid "661bfcf4-d5c1-5b96-9534-b39e2fc11947" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186426862}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186426862 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186426857 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "06febdbc-65f9-5901-99f7-6a7827495ba9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x\\notin \\text{Span}\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2}\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426843} {:answer/id #uuid "5fac1657-f0bf-58cd-839a-2936f55e9617" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426846} {:answer/id #uuid "922920ae-5499-5f5e-8c1f-2a7d78b98e5b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426848} {:answer/id #uuid "a26be051-5458-55a3-b657-078318cd500e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426849} {:answer/id #uuid "de386f32-9648-5557-95da-e81b5a893cdb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426852}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186426849} :answer-field/id #uuid "6dbd70cc-1860-587f-a06b-f6be24d7a7e1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426855}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "ad22bfb4-da83-594b-af3c-ca1a05478310" :question/math-academy-id "q-112247" :question/problem "Find the coordinates of the vector $x$ relative to the basis $B=\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2}\\},$ where\n\n$$\n{b}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}],\\,{b}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 9\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]$ then what is the value of ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}?$" :question/worked-solution "We need to find ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{b}_{1}+{x}_{2}{b}_{2} & =x \\\\ {x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 9\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe equation above gives the system with the augmented matrix\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 2 \\\\ -3 & 1 & 9\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nRow-reducing the matrix using Gaussian elimination, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 2 \\\\ -3 & 1 & 9\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -5 & 15\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-2{x}_{2}=2 \\\\ -5{x}_{2}=15.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get ${x}_{2}=-3.$ Substituting this into the first equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}-2(-3)=2\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=-4.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}].$\n\nFinally, ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=(-4)+(-3)=-7.$"} :step/id #uuid "f56d58dc-6376-5d83-8bb7-3af73050ef21" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186426859}}] :activity/title "Expressing the Coordinates of a Vector in a Given Basis" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426842}] [{:activity/course {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186046658} :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186455517} :activity/id #uuid "dd948f84-01c7-51cf-b5c9-f9c00a2b84b8" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050638 :topic/id #uuid "5ae18ce0-90c2-55f7-8d81-bd5949f05aa3" :topic/math-academy-id 1864} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186455516 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186455442 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "066bb7c4-7521-5727-993a-55db17b87282" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454919} {:answer/id #uuid "49378edd-134f-5712-a720-7f1c131c32c8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186455026} {:answer/id #uuid "a6f74b12-935c-5e33-a5e5-220baef222b1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x\\notin \\text{Span}\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{b}_{3}\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186455198} {:answer/id #uuid "b4852b6d-9a78-5d08-bc44-0fc169587a8b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186455217} {:answer/id #uuid "f9fc417c-d758-5208-baf3-43da35bca066" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186455333}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186455333} :answer-field/id #uuid "8aa3925e-da8c-56e5-b9b6-c047f1edb4c2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186455385}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "3d89aeef-7acc-5575-9764-44e144045f82" :question/math-academy-id "q-75998" :question/problem "Find the coordinates of the vector $x$ relative to the basis $B=\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{b}_{3}\\},$ where\n\n$$\n{b}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],\\,{b}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],\\,{b}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 11 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]$ then what is the value of ${x}_{1}?$" :question/worked-solution "We need to find ${x}_{1}$,  ${x}_{2}$, and ${x}_{3}$ such that  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{b}_{1}+{x}_{2}{b}_{2}+{x}_{3}{b}_{3} & =x \\\\ {x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{3}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 11 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom this, we get the system with the augmented matrix $M$, which we reduce using Gaussian elimination: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M= & [\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 1 & 6 \\\\ 3 & 2 & 1 & 11 \\\\ 2 & 2 & -1 & -6\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\ ∼ & [\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 1 & 6 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -2 & 7 \\\\ 2 & 2 & -1 & -6\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-2){R}_{2} \\\\ ∼ & [\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 1 & 6 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -2 & -7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -3 & -6\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}=6 \\\\ -{x}_{2}-2{x}_{3}=-7 \\\\ -3{x}_{3}=-6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the third equation, we get ${x}_{3}=2.$ Substituting this into the second   equation yields\n\n$$\n-{x}_{2}-2(2)=-7\\,⟹\\,{x}_{2}=3.\n$$\n\n Finally,  by substituting ${x}_{2}=3$ and ${x}_{3}=2$ into the first equation we obtain\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}+(3)+2=6\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].$\n\nSo, we have ${x}_{1}=1.$"} :step/id #uuid "3120d902-59cf-52cd-afde-5f7a4f7e1d5f" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186455531}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186455517 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120352 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "028867b0-8cf6-524a-93e6-8e63fa02e23d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186317580} {:answer/id #uuid "2f329de5-7c1a-5fad-b2d2-f7cc8384731d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186317709} {:answer/id #uuid "5f5bbc70-a2a7-5d4f-9c69-50122cef639d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186317888} {:answer/id #uuid "844d0795-32e6-5eb9-9815-e5906f5fb3e2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318014} {:answer/id #uuid "c5c361cd-49f5-527f-91c1-eb17cbe67bc5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x\\notin \\text{Span}\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2}\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186455244}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186317580} :answer-field/id #uuid "add90972-43b4-50ff-b652-f7e992bc2ad7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318801}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "f17a8e42-194f-52ed-9136-123dd348b4bc" :question/math-academy-id "q-34617" :question/problem "Find the coordinates of the vector $x$ relative to the basis $B=\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2}\\},$ where\n\n$$\n{b}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}],\\,{b}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]$ then what is the value of ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}?$" :question/worked-solution "We need to find ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{b}_{1}+{x}_{2}{b}_{2} & =x \\\\ {x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe equation above gives the system with the augmented matrix\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 1 & 6\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nRow-reducing the matrix using Gaussian elimination, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 1 & 6\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 10\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}=2 \\\\ 5{x}_{2}=10.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get ${x}_{2}=2.$ Substituting this into the first equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}+2(2)=2\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=-2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].$\n\nFinally, ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=(-2)+2=0.$"} :step/id #uuid "3d7897f3-95d9-53e4-9b05-08455a50a2b6" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186455528}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186455527 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186409819 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2115aac5-da66-5510-8b11-176ba754f81a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186409789} {:answer/id #uuid "45dbc0e6-16a9-5c62-a183-2dd30e767a3a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186409790} {:answer/id #uuid "60013665-0a5a-5449-9017-6cb6ae7ed2ca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186409792} {:answer/id #uuid "7ad6f309-f775-5604-ba46-fa9609a5688b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186409798} {:answer/id #uuid "ba977b58-8add-5c57-ae69-640a36ab4ef9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186409803}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186409792} :answer-field/id #uuid "fe323417-1cf2-5a08-b6a1-9d36f7d769a5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186409816}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "d9b245f0-31aa-56fe-aa26-5663dd9e140f" :question/math-academy-id "q-112211" :question/problem "Find the coordinates of the vector $x$ relative to the basis $B=\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2}\\},$ where\n\n$$\n{b}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,{b}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}-7 \\\\ -8 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]$ then what is the value of ${x}_{2}?$" :question/worked-solution "Remember, the order of the vectors in a basis is important.\n\nNotice that \n\n$$\n{{[\\begin{aligned}-7 \\\\ -8 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{x}={{(\\,-8\\,)}_{⏟}}_{{x}_{1}}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{b}_{1}}+{{(\\,-7\\,)}_{⏟}}_{{x}_{2}}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{b}_{2}}\n$$\n\nwhich means that\n\n$$\nx=(-8)\\cdot {b}_{1}+(-7)\\cdot {b}_{2}\n$$\n\nand therefore\n\n$$\n[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}-8 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFinally, we have that ${x}_{2}=-7.$"} :step/id #uuid "af36c254-27dd-5c17-9617-e7f9d654737f"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186455528 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186319175 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "28f401e4-eb59-5198-abf4-1458830b331c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186317692} {:answer/id #uuid "55e9e214-e0b3-5771-95e7-5cb487ad7118" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186317852} {:answer/id #uuid "914f6ffc-e4c9-5161-9fde-b475bcf8fceb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318060} {:answer/id #uuid "e0273188-6c7e-5354-921c-cdc4386a3d9a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318313} {:answer/id #uuid "32fd85ec-3fca-5fdb-8d41-028482470a84" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x\\notin \\text{span}\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2}\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454982}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186317852} :answer-field/id #uuid "e0750bff-0d7b-54f9-bc9f-9e5f7a657747" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318894}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "706ae806-e20f-56d6-9072-359885047529" :question/math-academy-id "q-34738" :question/problem "Find the coordinates of the vector $x$ relative to the basis $B=\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2}\\},$ where\n\n$$\n{b}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,{b}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}],\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ -8 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]$ then what is the value of ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}?$" :question/worked-solution "We need to find ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{b}_{1}+{x}_{2}{b}_{2} & =x \\\\ {x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ -8 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe equation above gives the system with the augmented matrix \n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 4 & 6 \\\\ 5 & 2 & -8 \\\\ 0 & -3 & -3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nRow-reducing the matrix using Gaussian elimination, we obtain the following: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M= & [\\begin{aligned}-1 & 4 & 6 \\\\ 5 & 2 & -8 \\\\ 0 & -3 & -3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+5{R}_{1} \\\\ ∼ & [\\begin{aligned}-1 & 4 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 22 & 22 \\\\ 0 & -3 & -3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+\\frac{3}{22}{R}_{2} \\\\ ∼ & [\\begin{aligned}-1 & 4 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 22 & 22 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}-{x}_{1}+4{x}_{2}=6 \\\\ 22{x}_{2}=22.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get ${x}_{2}=1.$ Substituting this into the first equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n-{x}_{1}+4(1)=6\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=-2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$ \n\nFinally, ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=-2+1=-1.$"} :step/id #uuid "bc51db51-8852-5a95-a4d4-b77331fb8d8a" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186455516}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186455531 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186455505 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2679ade7-de7e-5ff4-88c8-94968abbecd0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454962} {:answer/id #uuid "2e4e66c0-8e5c-5dff-8789-8ac0302fb04b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454974} {:answer/id #uuid "58225722-5487-53b4-b242-37a168921893" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186455056} {:answer/id #uuid "a19f8251-ccaa-52d8-8b83-bba63f64cb63" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x\\notin \\text{Span}\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{b}_{3}\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186455191} {:answer/id #uuid "f7cbfdfe-250f-5f75-93f6-f1ca311bd2d2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186455327}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186454962} :answer-field/id #uuid "8c6024f5-9069-597b-a291-cd59361ac136" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186455386}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "e3764343-10e9-5a7d-b034-e095faf7f51c" :question/math-academy-id "q-76054" :question/problem "Find the coordinates of the vector $x$ relative to the basis $B=\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{b}_{3}\\},$ where\n\n$$\n{b}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],\\,{b}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{b}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 15 \\\\ 12\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]$ then what is the value of ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}?$" :question/worked-solution "We need to find ${x}_{1}$,  ${x}_{2}$, and ${x}_{3}$ such that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{b}_{1}+{x}_{2}{b}_{2}+{x}_{3}{b}_{3} & =x \\\\ {x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{3}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 15 \\\\ 12\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom this, we get the system with the augmented matrix $M$, which we reduce using Gaussian elimination: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M= & [\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 3 & 15 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 0 & 12\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\ ∼ & [\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 3 & 15 \\\\ 0 & 4 & -3 & 3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-2){R}_{2} \\\\ ∼ & [\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 3 & 15 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -9 & -27\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}=3 \\\\ 2{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3}=15 \\\\ -9{x}_{3}=-27.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the third equation, we get ${x}_{3}=3.$ Substituting this into the second   equation yields\n\n$$\n2{x}_{2}+3(3)=15\\,⟹\\,{x}_{2}=3.\n$$\n\n Finally,  by substituting ${x}_{2}=3$ and ${x}_{3}=3$ into the first equation we obtain\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}-3+3=3\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=3.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].$\n\nSo, we have \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}=3+3+3=9.\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "e175e73c-1506-54af-ab5d-d11256d84f83" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186455527}}] :activity/title "Expressing the Coordinates of a Vector in a Given Basis" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454902}]}
